Seeded defect for tests/BLite.Tests/Oracles/WalCrashTests.cs

Hand-made: the group commit writer acknowledges a batch without flushing the WAL
(StorageEngine.GroupCommit.cs, ProcessBatchAsync drops `await _wal.FlushAsync()`). The commit
records stay in the WAL's 64 KB stream buffer, CommitAsync returns, and the pages the commit
stopped using are freed in the page file at once. A process that dies before the buffer fills
loses commits it acknowledged, and the documents they replaced come back with overflow pages
that are already on the free list.

With it applied, rows that pass on upstream 0450b97 fail, e.g. ProcessCrash / Durability
(123 of 492 crash states), ProcessCrash / Pages.Reachable, ProcessCrash / Continue,
TornWrite / Atomicity and TornWrite / Durability. ProcessCrash / Pages.Reachable shrinks to:
    1. Insert(id=74, count=3, code=c08, payload=18000 chars)
    2. Backup
    3. Upsert(id=74, count=7, code=null, payload=20 chars)
  crash after FreePage(24): page 24 written during step 3: page 24, on the overflow chain of
  the document at page 25, slot 0, has type Free

Reproduce: git apply tests/BLite.Tests/Oracles/Seeds/WalCrashTests.ack-before-wal-flush.patch && dotnet test tests/BLite.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~WalCrashTests
Restore:   git checkout -- src

The source file uses CRLF line endings; apply with --ignore-whitespace if the patch was
normalised. Never commit the seeded state.

